@gateway = http://localhost:5080
@timesheet = http://localhost:5082

### Sign in first
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@company.com",
  "password": "Demo@123"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Connect a provider — no user id in the body; the token decides whose account
POST {{gateway}}/api/integrations/connect
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "GitHub",
  "accessToken": "demo-token-github"
}

### Connection status, including any last sync error
GET {{gateway}}/api/integrations/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Generate this week. Any date in the week works — the server snaps it to Monday,
### and running it twice replaces the week rather than duplicating it.
POST {{gateway}}/api/timesheets/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "weekStartDate": "2026-09-02"
}

### The caller's own timesheets
GET {{gateway}}/api/timesheets/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Someone else's timesheets -> 403
GET {{gateway}}/api/timesheets/user/2c6b9a04-57e3-4f81-b3d7-0a94e2f16c58
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Approving your own timesheet as an employee -> 403 (was 204 before this release)
POST {{gateway}}/api/approvals/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approve": true
}

### Ask the assistant about your own activity — no user id in the body
POST {{gateway}}/api/chat/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What did I work on last Thursday?"
}

### Manager-only: pending approvals for the calling manager's team
GET {{gateway}}/api/approvals/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health
GET {{timesheet}}/health
